[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2809181812","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105336#issuecomment-2809181812","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105336","id":2809181812,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ncLZ0","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-16T10:43:06Z","updated_at":"2025-04-16T10:43:06Z","body":"I suspect at some point this is caused by this implementation in the Wayland DisplayServer\n\n```cpp\nint DisplayServerWayland::window_get_current_screen(DisplayServer::WindowID p_window_id) const {\n\t// Standard Wayland APIs don't support getting the screen of a window.\n\treturn 0;\n}\n```\n\nThe 0th screen would be your small monitor but because this is unimplemented despite your window being in the 2nd monitor we default to the 1st (incorrect) monitor.\n\nI believe an interesting place is `Window::popup`. There are a lot of calls to `set_position` there and a lot of dependence on the screen information being valid, which on Wayland it is not. In fact, almost all windows will be erroneously set to screen 0 regardless of the one they are actually in (see `Window::get_current_screen`). If any of the many calls to popup use information about their containing screen (which many do) they are liable for placing things in the wrong position.\n\nI do not have an explanation for why this would be a regression from 4.4 onwards and doesn't affect 4.3 which should have wayland too. No explanation for why only the x position seems fine (maybe it's in a VBoxContainer?) either.\n\nAs far as any other tests if you set you monitor configuration to not be symmetric (eg left monitor down, right up) do you get clamping where both top and bottom popups are clamped to the bounds of the 2 or does it only follow what the left monitor does?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2809181812/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816474272","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105336#issuecomment-2816474272","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105336","id":2816474272,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n3_yg","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T02:24:31Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T02:24:31Z","body":"Hi, thank you for the report!\n\nAre you using the opt-in Wayland display driver or the default X11 driver? If you're not sure, it should be enough to open the editor, look for the \"Help > Copy system info\" option in the top bar and pasting from the clipboard here.\n\n@ArchercatNEO\n\n> I believe an interesting place is Window::popup. There are a lot of calls to set_position there and a lot of dependence on the screen information being valid, which on Wayland it is not.\n\nDon't worry, I thought of everything ;) That's why I have added a new `DisplaySever` feature flag for the Wayland driver called `FEATURE_SELF_FITTING_WINDOWS` which lets nodes know to not try to be smart with windows. Look in `scene/main/window.cpp` and `scene/gui/popup.cpp` to see how we avoid relying on this missing information.\n\nExactly because of this special case, I have a feeling that what we might be seeing is either the Wayland driver running on a faulty compositor (which should be reported upstream) or, most likely, the X11 backend having issues with window fitting for whatever reason (XWayland quirks?).\n\nThat's why I'd like to make sure what driver OP is using.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816474272/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816617043","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105336#issuecomment-2816617043","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105336","id":2816617043,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n4ipT","user":{"login":"TylerSwan","id":79604863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NjA0ODYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79604863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan","html_url":"https://github.com/TylerSwan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T08:53:54Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T08:54:51Z","body":"@ArchercatNEO \n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/811947d4-6d4e-4fa3-829b-511235e680fb)\n\nThis is actually the worst of both worlds as it now clamps on the top and bottom, so the only valid screen space is the area the left and right monitor share in common with the middle monitor.\n\nI think that's what you asked for?\n\n@Riteo \n\nGodot v4.4.1.stable - Garuda Linux #1 ZEN SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Sun, 23 Mar 2025 17:17:17 +0000 on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2080 (nvidia; 570.133.07) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-8700K CPU @ 3.70GHz (12 threads)\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816617043/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816619090","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105336#issuecomment-2816619090","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105336","id":2816619090,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n4jJS","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T09:01:13Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T09:01:13Z","body":"Yes, that is what I asked for thanks for doing that. It means it's certainly doing something with many monitors not just assuming something with the first one.\n\n@TylerSwan from within a terminal could you start godot with the `--display-driver wayland` flag?\nYour system is wayland capable but godot is still running under xwayland here. That could help pinpoint if it's a problem in the X11 display server or elsewhere.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816619090/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816624076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105336#issuecomment-2816624076","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105336","id":2816624076,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n4kXM","user":{"login":"TylerSwan","id":79604863,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc5NjA0ODYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/79604863?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan","html_url":"https://github.com/TylerSwan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TylerSwan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T09:12:18Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T09:13:23Z","body":"@ArchercatNEO \n\nI am unable to re-create the bug after booting with those flags, so that seems like a success. Tried top offset, bottom offset, and staggered, all windows are aligning to the bounds of the monitor they live on in each case.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816624076/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816626100","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105336#issuecomment-2816626100","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105336","id":2816626100,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6n4k20","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-19T09:18:43Z","updated_at":"2025-04-19T09:18:43Z","body":"Well that's good news for the wayland DisplayServer. FYI, the wayland session is still not the default, those flags force godot to use the Wayland DisplayServer which handles this stuff diferently. That it works on wayland and this is a regression that means the fault is almost certainly in the X11 DisplayServer.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2816626100/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]